<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">14 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 14 February, from 278 to 1989.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">278 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,748 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Traditional date of the martyrdom of Saint Valentine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Tradition holds that Valentine, a priest or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a> of Terni, was beheaded on the Via Flaminia outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. His link with romantic love dates only from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, notably the poetry of Chaucer.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/842">842 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,184 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Oaths of Strasbourg sworn by Charlemagne's grandsons</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> pledged alliance against their brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a>, each swearing in the other's language. The oaths are the earliest surviving text in a form of French.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oaths-of-strasbourg">Oaths of Strasbourg</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charlemagne">Charlemagne</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1400">1400 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">626 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Deposed Richard II dies at Pontefract Castle</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Richard II, overthrown by his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-of-england">Henry Bolingbroke</a> in 1399, died in captivity around this date, probably starved to death. His fall sowed the dynastic rivalry behind the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1779">1779 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">247 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Captain James Cook is killed in Hawaii</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Cook died in a clash with Hawaiians at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kealakekua-bay">Kealakekua Bay</a> after trying to take a chief hostage over a stolen boat. His three voyages had charted much of the Pacific.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1876">1876 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">150 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander Graham Bell files his telephone patent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Bell's lawyer filed his application at the US Patent Office on the same day that <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elisha">Elisha</a> Gray filed a caveat for a similar device. Bell's patent was granted in March and upheld in long litigation.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell">Alexander Graham Bell</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1929">1929 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">97 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Saint Valentine's Day Massacre in Chicago</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Gunmen, some dressed as police, shot dead seven men linked to Bugs Moran's gang in a garage. The killings, widely blamed on Al Capone, turned public opinion against gangland violence.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1946">1946 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">80 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">ENIAC is unveiled at the University of Pennsylvania</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The US Army publicly revealed ENIAC, the first programmable general-purpose electronic computer. With nearly 18,000 vacuum tubes, it could perform 5,000 additions a second.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1989">1989 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">37 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ayatollah Khomeini issues a fatwa against Salman Rushdie</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>'s leader called on Muslims to kill the author of 'The Satanic Verses' and his publishers. Rushdie spent years in hiding; translators and publishers were attacked, and he was stabbed in 2022.</p></div></li></ol>
